{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Pure McCartney Deluxe feels like a natural next choice because my Beatles listening gives me a specific connection to his songs.",
    "The Motown originals, Grease soundtrack, and Queen-associated Bohemian Rhapsody appeal to my interest in familiar older songs, while Roberta Flack fits the gentler listening reflected in Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Ultimate Collection, Gold, and The River do not give me enough information to connect them to an artist or songs I enjoy; I would pass because the musical fit is uncertain.",
    "Love Stuff and Let Them Talk do not give me the same immediate connection to familiar pop and rock favorites, which is what I want to revisit today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A greatest-hits or collection title alone seems to count too much; I choose collections because of the artists and songs they contain.",
    "My varied listening seems to have been taken as interest in unfamiliar albums, even though much of my history points toward returning to known favorites."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between the Beatles and McCartney matters more to me than a broad resemblance between album titles.",
    "My repeated interest in best-of collections and older hits reflects a desire for recognizable songs, with room for both classic rock and gentler melodic music."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The choices partly capture my interest in nostalgic favorites, but some rely on broad collection cues without a clear connection to music I know."
}"}
